}}|subdivision_type1=[[Communities of Balisca|Community]]|subdivision_name1={{flag|Cerdanya}}|area_km2=28713.55|population_census=4,792,897|population_census_year=2025|regional_languages=|common_languages=[[Mozbayani]], [[Baliscano]], {{W|Catalan language|Volisanian}}, {{W|Occitan language|Beron}} and [[Walldungu language|Walldungu]]|cctld=.mta|government_type={{W|Liquid democracy}}|mapsize=280px|ethnic_groups_year=2023|ethnic_groups=68.6% [[Baliscans]]<br/> 31.4% [[Demographics of Balisca|others]]|population_census_rank=12th}}'''Muntanya''' (Volisanian pronunciation: {{W|IPA|/monˈtaɲa/, [mõn̪ˈt̪a.ɲa]''}}) is a landlocked [[Regions of Balisca|region]] in central [[Cerdanya]], within the [[Baliscan Confederation]]. It borders the [[Dríadas]] to the north, [[Arcadia]] to the southeast, [[Abellesia]] to the southwest and [[Provence]] to the west. It has an area of {{convert|28713.55|km2|mi2|abbr=on}} making it the # largest region of Balisca, and a population of 4,792,897 in the [[2025 Baliscan census|2025 census]]. The administrative seat is [[Poble]].

The area that became Muntanya was first inhabited by groups of hunter–gatherers 13,000 years ago. The predominant indigenous population prior to the arrival of Illypnians were the [[Wallche people]]. Muntanya was colonized relatively late in comparison to other regions of Balisca, beginning with the establishment of Poble in 1714.  

